3,000 requests per phase; the primary's error rate in each:
  healthy 1%, flaky 25%, down 100%, recovered 1%
a cooldown is counted in requests

  breaker                            healthy      flaky       down  recovered
                                  waste / fb waste / fb waste / fb waste / fb
  no breaker                           1 / 1    24 / 24  100 / 100      1 / 1
  3 failures in a row, cool 50         1 / 1    13 / 56    2 / 100      1 / 1
  10 failures in a row, cool 50        1 / 1    24 / 24    2 / 100      1 / 1
  over 20% of last 20, cool 50         1 / 1     7 / 77    2 / 100      1 / 2
  over 50% of last 20, cool 50         1 / 1    25 / 25    2 / 100      1 / 1

waste: % of requests that failed on the primary first (each costs its latency)
fb: % answered by the fallback model (each is a different model's answer)
